1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:04,816
The Scope of a Conclusion Our research team examined a global trend

2
00:00:04,829 --> 00:00:10,145
over a ten-year span An apparent similarity between two regions was notable

3
00:00:10,368 --> 00:00:14,842
but the differences were equally important We divided the data into a

4
00:00:14,855 --> 00:00:19,026
segment for each period and checked whether simultaneous changes had a shared

5
00:00:19,039 --> 00:00:24,434
explanation A figure of nought did not necessarily prove absence it might

6
00:00:24,447 --> 00:00:28,842
reflect the way a variable was recorded Nor did a dramatic peak

7
00:00:28,855 --> 00:00:34,342
justify an indefinite forecast The teacher asked us to qualify each inference

8
00:00:34,355 --> 00:00:39,816
and identify whether a result was statistically useful or merely interesting We

9
00:00:39,829 --> 00:00:44,737
could deem the findings suggestive without presenting them as final The overall

10
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:49,895
range remained broad and a peripheral factor might still matter Research should

11
00:00:49,908 --> 00:00:53,974
bring uncertainty to the fore rather than hide it To pore over

12
00:00:53,987 --> 00:00:58,934
evidence is worthwhile when it makes a conclusion more precise Its value

13
00:00:58,947 --> 00:01:02,605
lies not in sounding formidable but in saying exactly what the data

14
00:01:02,618 --> 00:01:03,474
can support
